# Training experiments — keep PLAN.md, RECOMMENDATIONS.md, and results/
# (text/metrics/plots), ignore raw datasets and large intermediate
# artifacts. See docs/claude/training-improvement-workflow.md.
# Pattern: re-include directories first so git recurses into them, then
# allow specific text files; finally re-ignore large binary formats
# inside results/.
experiments/**/*
!experiments/**/
!experiments/**/PLAN.md
!experiments/**/RECOMMENDATIONS.md
!experiments/**/SUMMARY.md
!experiments/**/*.py
!experiments/**/results/**/*.json
!experiments/**/results/**/*.md
!experiments/**/results/**/*.png
!experiments/**/results/**/*.svg
!experiments/**/results/**/*.txt

# Recombination sweep outputs (research-only artifacts; regenerated per run).
# See scripts/ops/recombination_sweep.py + docs/research/strategy-primitives-recombination-DESIGN.md.
results/recombination/

# Don't track bytecode under the re-included reports dirs
scripts/reports/__pycache__/

# M28 backtest candles — regenerated per run by scripts/macro/fetch_macro_candles.py (not committed)
data/macro_candles/

# Guard self-test probes (scripts/ci/guard_selftests.py). The planted-failure
# design is deliberate and must not be weakened — a guard nobody has seen fail
# is indistinguishable from one that cannot fire. What is NOT deliberate is
# where a probe lands: `_planted` cleans up on normal exit AND on exceptions,
# but by construction cannot on SIGKILL, a runner timeout, or a cancelled
# workflow. `selftest_diagnostic_provenance` must write its probe to a path the
# guard actually scans (it resolves the file from the diff, repo-relative), so
# unlike the deploy/ probe it cannot simply be moved to a temp dir. Ignoring it
# closes the remaining hole: a stranded copy is then unstageable by `git add -A`
# — the idiom this repo's sessions use constantly.
# Measured 2026-08-17: a stranded copy fails NO guard (run_guards PASS 42), so
# committing it was the whole risk. BL-20260817-GUARD-SELFTESTS-PLANT-PROBE-FILES-IN-THE-LIVE-REPO-TREE
scripts/ml/_selftest_probe.py

# E2 horizon-arm sweep outputs (research-only; regenerated per run by
# .github/workflows/research-e2-horizon-arm.yml, which uploads them as a build
# artifact instead). Panels are ~10-30MB of JSONL per (symbol, horizon) rung, so
# they are reproduced from the committed workflow + the public feed, never stored.
# NOTE the path is deliberately artifacts/research/ and NOT artifacts/ — this repo
# genuinely tracks artifacts/health/ (5 files), and a blanket ignore would make
# those unstageable by the `git add -A` idiom these sessions use constantly.
artifacts/research/
